", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c806adc0b45db41a1004dff0644358c80466a791", "message": "Add elog-3.1.5_p20230218-r1", "created_at": "2023-09-07T09:02:39Z", "repo": "kangie-tools", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8218d9b1969c023f8771004c87ad933c4db7f692", "message": "Proper thunderbolt support", "created_at": "2021-08-18T07:44:21Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7d7da2a772bd266aef633af4c3caaa7d9b1a6f43", "message": "Enable terminus font (hidpi)", "created_at": "2021-08-14T04:10:22Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2f69e0bc8c116610361f52b3c2c5e6ad747f508e", "message": "Add XPS 15 9560 (5.13.8)", "created_at": "2021-08-10T06:12:48Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "239062d190c848bb9ccf6b4bcbc093dfa9fa3db7", "message": "Add KVM built-in support", "created_at": "2021-02-27T12:50:16Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ead187d1a230b44edc3a0636ce0192325f9d5f69", "message": "Add 5.11.x config.\n\nWhole bunch of docker stuff enabled since 5.7.x", "created_at": "2021-02-25T05:05:06Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "161fec424219522c36c6c93033aa47f72bb46c5e", "message": "Dell: Latitude e5480: 5.7.2 kernel\n\nAll major functionality working as tested.\n\nUntested: Type-C docking capability.\n\nKnown Issues: PCIE AER errors on one port, potentially from WLAN card?", "created_at": "2020-06-12T10:39:44Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4803554dc3dceaa064830e66ed1f7ed284a6108e", "message": "Latitude: 7390 + e5470: Version Bump 5.7.0\n\nLatitude e5470:\nfanotify + fanotify permissions checking enabled (clamAV)\nNew exfat support\n\nLatitude 7390:\nNew exfat support\n\nMulti-line description of commit,\nfeel free to be detailed", "created_at": "2020-06-09T02:39:50Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6238072c17bca37a418dc2b16d23d0b6a04ff384", "message": "Latitude 7390: DW5816e WWAN\n\nEnable qmi_wwan (qmi comms) and qcserial (AT port, NMEA, DM).\nDrivers do not currently support DF5816, but patches have been submitted\nto kernel upstream, so this will build drivers when they're ready.", "created_at": "2020-05-04T14:33:46Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e5ed6a61edf0fba9afef12a9610120aa6e008014", "message": "Latitude 7390: version bump", "created_at": "2020-04-23T11:28:36Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7920d0ac05340568470f624b21b208b88464e827", "message": "Latitude 7390: i915 firmware, stack depth\n\nCONFIG_DEBUG_STACK_USAGE=N\nGentoo/Kernel default for some reason, it's a debug message. Ignore it.\n\ni915 firmware: i915/kbl_dmc_v1_04.bin, i915/kbl_guc_33.0.0.bin, i915/kbl_huc_4.0.0.bin\nPrevious issues caused by faulty hardware, re-enabling firmware.\nCommand line option \"i915.enable_guc=2\" will enable loading of guc and verification of huc firmware.", "created_at": "2020-04-23T11:24:18Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ca5485f0591093605740ce3ba63df1162af8737d", "message": "Latitude 7390: Coretemp driver", "created_at": "2020-04-21T11:24:21Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "76f9269619468b6ec894a5cb04ad0c7b65e0c3cb", "message": "Latitude 7390: Drivers and firmware\n\nDrivers:\nWebcam, Sound\nFirmware:\nWiFi regulatory.db\n-i915/kbl_dmc_ver1_04.bin - causes lockups and reboots. Hardare fault or bug?", "created_at": "2020-04-20T11:48:58Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5273460bccc18de849966aaaa1bee802a2dcd523", "message": "Dell Latitude 7390 - Initial Kernel\n\nMajor functionality working, some features to be enabled.\n\nVideo, Audio, WLAN, Ethernet, Touchscreen, Touchpad all working.\nWWAN enabled but not tested.", "created_at": "2020-04-17T13:38:40Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "72866154185c347c4896eb669be6d7956a20d336", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470: 5.6.2 version bump\n\nMicrosoft exfat driver moved to staging - enabled. Replace with samsung\ncode in 5.7.", "created_at": "2020-04-07T13:20:24Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "432a38ac86109b684d686025e54cd42f0ad35f83", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470: ALSA SoC Audio\n\nEnabled ALSA System on Chip layer.\nCONFIG_SND_SOC_INTEL_SKYLAKE=Y among other things.", "created_at": "2020-04-07T12:57:49Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d3b888fc99a891858499b5c510f12f86190eee60", "message": "Dell Latitude E5470: FUSE Support\n\nAdded FUSE support as a dependency of an app I'm using.\nCONFIG_FUSE_FS = Y", "created_at": "2020-04-07T05:26:11Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b176e60ccd2bae8d5073544779faf13154e55636", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470: intel_pch_thermal\n\nintel_pch_thermal = y", "created_at": "2020-04-04T13:37:30Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6aa37b8c13b11b07210223737093d89702d27669", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470: Intel Thermal Framework\n\nCONFIG_INT340X_THERMAL = Y", "created_at": "2020-04-04T13:16:11Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a684a6da3267bb0517e8ab69ac9f31c00b7475f4", "message": "Revert \"Dell Latitude e5470 - AppImage support\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5d0ec6e87a3e9d813ee3645929bb6004e1592bb6.\n\nRemoved - Will come back to it later on. AppImage works perfectly with\nFUSE support, but loader doesn't like the WINE image I'm using.", "created_at": "2020-04-04T12:16:59Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5d0ec6e87a3e9d813ee3645929bb6004e1592bb6", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470 - AppImage support\n\nEnabled:\nFUSE\nX32_ABI", "created_at": "2020-04-04T11:06:37Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "130863cc9b5093a2b812c6652c266d1304b08887", "message": "Dell Latitude e5470 - Additional hardware support\n\nRTS525A Card Reader (MISC_RTSX_PCI) = Y\nSunrise Point-LP PMC (INTEL_PMC_CORE) = Y", "created_at": "2020-04-04T09:42:03Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "aab29d6a4796cc8bc213f0067f34aaddbe0d776b", "message": "Huawei USB 4G modem support (e3372x)\n\nEnabled cdc-ether in kernel. Should probably be a module - I'll fix that\nwhen I work out if I need Huawei extensions.", "created_at": "2020-04-04T08:58:44Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "70015c5a37694e4de3ad536d7b344e4a0f82eaaf", "message": "Added Dell Latitude e5470 (Intel Integrated GPU)\n\nLatitude e5470 kernel configs with most features working (haven't tested\nsmartcard reader). May need to adjust config if you have the AMD GPU.", "created_at": "2020-03-30T06:23:24Z", "repo": "kernel-configs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b1c89b828176bc938273b085e5f9c01ab090df43", "message": "Initial Commit", "created_at": "2020-03-3